  },
  "description": "Aion 1.0 Instruct is a 2.3B-parameter open-weights small language model from the Microsoft Windows Applied Sciences Group, published on Hugging Face on 2026-11-18 as microsoft/Aion-1.0-Instruct-2.3B under the MIT license. It is the foundational on-device SLM for the Windows ecosystem and successor to Phi Silica, optimized for summarization, rewriting, chat, document comprehension, and tool calling at the edge. It is a dense causal decoder (28 layers, GQA, hybrid sliding-window plus full attention) with a 32,768-token context window and supports English, German, Spanish, Portuguese, Italian, French, Chinese, and Japanese. Microsoft says a further optimized version, paired with a content moderation model, will ship as the Windows OS SLM by the end of January 2027. No hosted API or gateway listing was available at catalog time. Benchmark scores are self-reported on the Hugging Face model card (EleutherAI lm-evaluation-harness where available).",
